	Introduction, Preface

	DirWorx will check your filelists and compare if the files in
	the list are present on your harddrive. If not it will replace
	the byte information about the file with DELETED. Simple ehh?

	Are you one of these lazy sysops which thinks it really sucks
	to go through your filelist and mark all files deleted? Well
	this door written in C will both do it fast and cool..?

	It will also save a log file which tells who runned the dir
	command and how much files & bytes which was removed.

	NOTE This door won't delete any of you files on your HD just
	     put deleted in front of the files in your filelist IF
	     they DO NOT EXIST on your harddrive :)

	Ofcourse can you choose which directory and a startdate :)

	NOTE! It is strongly recommended that you set this door to
	      a low security level so most users are able to run it
	      this way users could update your filelistnings incase
	      you've forgotten it! (The door is completly harmless
	      so their is no risc in letting them us it!)

